# RiceSearcher — local secrets/config (example).
#
# Copy to `credentials.env` (gitignored) and fill in. RiceSearcher loads
# `credentials.env` (then `.env`) from the current directory before running a
# command; an explicit shell `export` always wins over these files.

# Anthropic API key — used ONLY by the scorer (`ricesearcher score`). Nothing
# else in this project calls a paid API. Get one at https://console.anthropic.com/
# Uncomment and paste your real key. Left as the placeholder, `score` would send
# it and fail with a 401 authentication_error.
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-...

# Optional: override the scorer model (default: claude-haiku-4-5, the lowest-cost
# option at $1/$5 per 1M). Set a more capable/pricier model here if wanted.
# RICESEARCHER_SCORER_MODEL=claude-sonnet-4-6

# Beat profiles are chosen per command with `--profile ID`; there is no env var
# for them (RICESEARCHER_BEAT_PROFILE was retired by ADR-002).

# Optional: sentence-transformers model used by `dedup` (default: all-MiniLM-L6-v2).
# RICESEARCHER_EMBED_MODEL=all-MiniLM-L6-v2

# Optional: local data root (default: ~/.ricesearcher).
# RICESEARCHER_DATA_DIR=~/.ricesearcher

# Optional: override where beat-profile JSON files live (default:
# <data_dir>/profiles).
# RICESEARCHER_PROFILES_DIR=~/.ricesearcher/profiles

# Optional: RiceSearcher's own handoff root that RiceClipper pulls from (default:
# ~/ricesearcher-handoff). NOT ~/riceclipper-handoff (that's RiceClipper's output
# to RicePoster). RiceClipper reads this dir; must match RiceClipper's inbox setting.
# RICESEARCHER_HANDOFF_DIR=~/ricesearcher-handoff
